/ Task 27e-e: the wording advice for one field of the listing text editor. Advice, not a gate: nothing here
/ blocks a save or a publish. `warnings` are ListingCopyAdvisor::Warning structs for this field (the page
/ passes an empty list when the text is clean, and then nothing is drawn). The heading carries the meaning in
/ words, so colour is never the only signal.
- base = 'apps.listing_texts.show.advice'
- if warnings.any?
  .d-alert.d-alert-warning.dark:d-alert-soft.mt-2.text-xs role="note" id="listing-text-#{field}-advice"
    div
      p.font-semibold = t("#{base}.title")
      ul.list-disc.pl-4
        - warnings.each do |warning|
          li data-advice=warning.key = t("#{base}.warnings.#{warning.key}", match: warning.match.to_s, count: warning.count, limit: warning.limit)
